==German==
===Etymology===
Originally {{term||*Hebanne|lang=de}} from {{etyl|goh|de}} {{term|hevanna||midwife|lang=goh}}, later contorted to {{term||Hebamme|lang=de}} to resemble {{term|Amme||wet nurse|lang=de}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈheːpˌʔamə/|/ˈheːˌbamə/|lang=de}}

===Noun===
